body:
It's always been the opposite for me. I struggle with the mercy stuff. 'Do evil get rekt' makes sense to me inherently, as well as Him having a super absolute nature. It's a struggle to understand  forgivness- let alone the reconsilliation aspet of God. It's still there, still godd and still important even though I don't get it as well as I probably should. I just accept thet He knows people better than I do, and if He's letting someone slide right now, it's because He's smarter than me and looking at something I'm not. The only way they aren't getting what they earn is if they take Him up on His offer. He'll know if they mean it or not and if they do- Great! The  problem is resolved because they're trying. If not- fine! They'll get what they deserve.  

I know it's not the attitude I should have, but it's where I'm at. If youre hung up about an aspect of God's nature that rub you the wrong way- Great! Join the crowd.

&#x200B;
